Criterion 4: did compositing turn any currently-passing pair into a failing one?

No. Every pair in theme_contrast_test.dart is opaque, and compositing is the
identity at alpha 1, so no ratio moved.

The proof is stronger than "the suite is green". Each of the 33 pairs in
theme_contrast_test.dart pins its measured ratio with `closeTo(pair.ratio,
0.01)` as well as asserting the AA/AAA floor, and this change edited NOT ONE of
those pinned numbers - the only edit to that file is the comment above the
opacity guard (see the real `git diff` below: 7 insertions, 3 deletions, all
comment). So a green run means every pair still measures the number it measured
before the fix.

The five painted-pixel ratios recorded in
docs/verification/issue-55/pixel-sample.log (14.63, 5.89, 5.22, 9.03, 16.67)
are additionally pinned as literals in
test/core/accessibility/accessibility_helpers_test.dart - see
criterion-2-opaque-pins.log.

